Small ReaxFF example and validation case: 5 short PEEK molecules (1030 atoms) simulated with
ReaxFF at 2000 K in LAMMPS; 3 frames (timesteps 0, 1000, 2000) in a single file.
PEEK_2000K.png shows a snapshot of the system.

The input file "bonds.reaxff.dump" was written with fix reaxff/bonds in LAMMPS. After the
header of each frame the file contains one line per atom with
- id = atom id
- type = atom type
- nb = number of bonds
- id_1 = atom id of first bond
- id_nb = atom id of Nth bond
- mol = molecule id
- bo_1 = bond order of first bond
- bo_nb = bond order of Nth bond
- abo = atom bond order (sum of all bonds)
- nlp = number of lone pairs
- q = atomic charge

Expected result for rxn_bond_cutoff in {0, 1, 2}: exactly 1 reaction at timestep 2000,
formation of the bond 703-719 (no bond broken).

Usage:
  from atomigraph import AtomiGraph
  ag = AtomiGraph(infile="examples/02_PEEK_one_reaction/bonds.reaxff.dump",
                  atom_type_map="1:C,2:H,3:H,4:O,5:O,6:O,7:O,8:O")
  ag.read()
  ag.find_reactions()
